#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:2 08b33bda149c4ac69583afa49d75e68f
msgid "Adding and removing drives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:4 d14b90dba7264f2eb34bd703da774a53
msgid ""
"A library's drives are part of its configuration, so adding or removing "
"one rewrites ``device.conf`` and restarts the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:12 f8ef836e80604feaaa53571973696c9e
msgid "Adding a drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:14 da3931210bf443498b70f7fcff9f3958
msgid ""
"**Operator → Add Drive**, or **Drives → Add a drive** on the library "
"page, which arrives with the library already chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:17 8640190ae0624540bb5b6d1861a6f0a8
msgid ""
"The page shows what the drive will be before you commit to it: the model,"
" the serial it will be given, the slot it will occupy, and its SCSI "
"address. Change the library and all of that changes with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:21 4a8b7a7bb2cb4a1abf72200c12d2a158
msgid ""
"Only drives this library's model takes are offered - plus any model the "
"library already holds, because a library on a real host does not always "
"match its profile, and refusing a drive identical to the ones already in "
"it would help nobody."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:26 a457536acd9e4f0cb44d0c8ad40d96a9
msgid "Add Drive: the models this library takes, and where the drive will go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:39 13d302e0384c40bb9a7f367a3d2a439a
msgid ""
"The slot, the drive id and the SCSI target are chosen for you: they are "
"the next free ones. Overriding them is not offered, because a drive at an"
" address something else already uses will not start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:44 2b01faaf89804acab8c4cbef7ff6f5f9
msgid "Removing a drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:46 5467bec7b130424b9612e18ab64c503b
msgid ""
"**Operator → Remove Drive**, or **Drives → Remove a drive** on the "
"library page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:49 e4bb64faaf2c4ca89faace14f59dcea0
msgid ""
"The page says what is in the drive before you remove it. A drive holding "
"a tape has that tape put back in its slot first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:52 36c06f4a7830417b98c1acb6dacf5d74
msgid "Remove Drive: which drive, and what it is holding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:63 77e149700a934d87b2aa01869b1de0f8
msgid ""
"This cannot be undone, although the drive can be added again. What it "
"removes is the drive's entry in ``device.conf``; no tape is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:67 1e4ac8f894974a2b9caad82c1c3b2d62
msgid "What it does to the running library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:69 78f1689cc117451bb628b9560cd5ad87
msgid ""
"Both restart the library, because MHVTL reads ``device.conf`` once, when "
"a daemon starts. Until it restarts, its robot reports the drives it had "
"when it started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:73 010485bfbd6041f8803b9aeb4e322bd0
msgid ""
"``--no-restart`` writes the configuration and leaves the daemons alone, "
"for when you are making several changes and want one restart at the end:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/drives.rst:82 2a6d8251f096423999b48fea1030f39e
msgid ""
"The console says the same thing, on the page: a library whose "
"configuration and whose robot disagree is flagged until it is restarted."
msgstr ""

